# Build context exclusions for the images that build from the REPOSITORY ROOT:
# gawk-admin and gawk-telemetry (both `replace` gawk-server, so their context
# has to span two modules — docs/42 D13), gawk-relay (it embeds the gawk-app
# build it serves, gawk-server/deploy/Dockerfile.relay — docs/76 §6.1), plus
# the dev stack's fakeidp and pubsim images. `gawk-app` builds from its own
# directory and has its own .dockerignore; `gawk-server` needs none.
#
# node_modules is here because leaving it out is a real, reproducible break,
# not tidiness. Both root-context UI stages do (and gawk-relay's app stage
# does the same with gawk-app/):
#
#     COPY <component>/ui/package.json <component>/ui/package-lock.json ./
#     RUN npm ci
#     COPY <component>/ui/ ./
#
# (both also copy common-ts/oidc-session/ the same way, docs/55 D3 — a
# directory that must stay IN this context; nothing here excludes it.)
#
# so a node_modules in the working tree is copied OVER the one `npm ci` just
# built — with the host's ownership and permission bits. On a machine where
# those bits do not survive the copy, the build dies at `sh: tsc: Permission
# denied`, which names neither the cause nor the fix. Anyone who has run
# `npm ci` before `docker compose up` hits it.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded here, unlike gawk-app's:
#
#   *.md     — the admin, telemetry and relay images COPY their
#              THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md into the final stage. Attribution
#              ships with the binary.
#   dist     — each Dockerfile's `COPY --from=ui` lands after the source copy
#              and overwrites a locally-built bundle, so a stale one cannot
#              reach the image. gawk-relay's stage.sh empties
#              cmd/gawk-relay/webapp/dist before it stages the app stage's
#              build, to the same effect.
**/node_modules
